// D12/D17 (multi-visit S4): UNSCHEDULED = no live visits, SCHEDULED = visits exist and none has
// started, IN_PROGRESS = any visit started. Those three are DERIVED server-side from the visit set
// (lib/job-status.ts) and written as a cache in the same transaction as any visit write; COMPLETED
// and CANCELLED are explicit, human-set, and never derived. Spec B1's unordered rule survives -
// every status stays reachable from every other.
//
// EN_ROUTE and ON_SITE RETIRED here: being on the way and being on site are properties of a TRIP,
// not of a job, and they live on VisitStatus. Existing rows in those two states migrated to
// IN_PROGRESS in 20260819120000_visit_lifecycle_multi_visit_s4.
enum JobStatus {
  UNSCHEDULED
